<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Transjordan</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – 1946 CE · capital Amman</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British-protected emirate of Abdullah east of the Jordan, the forerunner of the Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the French expelled his brother Faisal from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, Abdullah, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-bin-ali-king-of-hejaz">Sharif Husayn</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, arrived at Ma'an with followers in late 1920. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> conference of March 1921 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> agreed that he would govern the land east of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan">Jordan</a> under British mandate, separate from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mandatory-palestine">Mandatory Palestine</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Abdullah built a state from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> tribes and small towns, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amman">Amman</a> his capital. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> controlled finance and foreign affairs and funded the Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a>, built up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-peake">Frederick Peake</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-glubb">John Glubb</a>. The 1922 mandate memorandum excluded Transjordan from the provisions for a Jewish national home. A 1928 treaty and organic law established a legislative council.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> recognised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>'s independence by the Treaty of London of March 1946, and on 25 May Abdullah was proclaimed king of what became, from 1949, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan">Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-transjordan.jpg" alt="Emirate of Transjordan" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Emirate_of_Transjordan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – 1946 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Amman</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullah I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Transjordan, Emirate of Trans-Jordan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=emirate-of-transjordan" aria-label="Emirate of Transjordan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5605 1015 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Transjordan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5925 1271L4997 651M5925 1271L5908 1277M5925 1271L5925 1271"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M5908 1277h0M5925 1271h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5925 1271h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5925 1271h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Amman. <a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=emirate-of-transjordan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
